It is Saturday afternoon.
I come back to my flat.
A small note is stuck to my door.
It is a notice from the post office.
I read the note carefully.
The language is very official.
It says there: 'Your shipment will be left at the parcel shop.'
I read the text one more time.
Which parcel shop is it exactly?
Mostly, my parcels are dropped off at a kiosk.
But this parcel shop is on the next street.
And from when can I collect the parcel?
Another sentence on the note explains it.
It says there: 'The parcel will be made ready on the next working day.'
So that means not until Monday.
Normally these shops are closed on Sunday.
I take the note off the door.
Then I put it in my pocket.
I unlock the door.
Then I go inside.
